[[White Balboan people|White Balboans]] are the largest group at approximately 40 per cent, significantly higher than the national average of 26 per cent, reflecting the Redilution programme's focus on the Jala highlands. The white population is concentrated in the affluent zones — [[Zona 3 (Sant Bart)|Zona 3]], [[Zona 4 (Sant Bart)|Zona 4]], [[Zona 6 (Sant Bart)|Zona 6]], and the developed portions of [[Zona 7 (Sant Bart)|Zona 7]] — and in the professional and government classes of the central zones.

[[Black Balboan people|Black Balboans]] at approximately 32 per cent are concentrated in the working-class southern zones — [[Zona 8 (Sant Bart)|Zona 8]], [[Zona 9 (Sant Bart)|Zona 9]], and [[Zona 10 (Sant Bart)|Zona 10]] — and in the industrial areas. The Black community's presence in Sant Bart dates to the plantation era, when enslaved and later freed workers were employed in the highland estates.

[[Mixed Balboan people|Mixed Balboans]] at approximately 18 per cent are distributed throughout the city, with particular concentrations in the middle-class zones.

The [[Birú people|Birú]] community, at approximately 2 per cent, is the smallest indigenous group. The Birú are concentrated in the upper slopes of [[Zona 7 (Sant Bart)|Zona 7]], where communities have persisted in relative isolation since the colonial period. Internal migration from rural highland areas has brought additional Birú residents to the city in recent decades.

== Economy ==

Sant Bart is the principal commercial and administrative centre of Jala Province. The city's economy is dominated by government services, finance, retail, and light manufacturing, with a significant industrial base in the southern zones.

The central business district ([[Zona 2 (Sant Bart)|Zona 2]]) contains the city's financial institutions, corporate headquarters, and professional services firms. The government district ([[Zona 1 (Sant Bart)|Zona 1]]) houses the provincial government, the comarca administration, and various national institutions that maintained a presence in the former capital after reunification.

The southern zones — [[Zona 8 (Sant Bart)|Zona 8]], [[Zona 9 (Sant Bart)|Zona 9]], [[Zona 10 (Sant Bart)|Zona 10]], and [[Zona 11 (Sant Bart)|Zona 11]] — contain the city's industrial base, including textiles, processed foodstuffs, basic metal goods, and light manufacturing. These industries were established during the Velásquez industrialisation programme of the 1880s and expanded during the rump state period. The far eastern zones ([[Zona 11 (Sant Bart)|Zona 11]] and [[Zona 12 (Sant Bart)|Zona 12]]) also contain significant warehousing and logistics facilities, serving the city's role as a transport hub.

The entertainment and retail district ([[Zona 1 (Sant Bart)|Zona 1]]) contains the city's principal shopping malls, entertainment venues, and cultural institutions, including the [[Sant Bart Opera House]] and the [[National History Museum of Balboa|National History Museum]].

The city's GDP is estimated at approximately $25 billion, representing roughly 40 per cent of the provincial GDP. GDP per capita is approximately $8,900, higher than the provincial average of $7,300 but lower than the national average, reflecting the city's mix of high-income professional and low-income working-class populations.

== Government ==

Sant Bart is governed by an elected {{w|mayor}} (''alcalde'') and a {{w|city council}} (''consell municipal''). The mayor serves a four-year term and has executive authority over municipal administration, planning, and major infrastructure. The current mayor is [[Jordi Puig i Bosch]] ([[Balboa People's Party|BPP]]).

The city council is composed of 21 councillors — 12 elected from each of the city's zones, plus 9 at-large members elected by the whole city. The council has authority over local services, planning, and community matters within each zone, while the mayor and city council retain authority over cross-zone issues including transport, major infrastructure, and economic development.

The city is the seat of the [[Governor of Jala Province]] and the [[Sant Bart (comarca)|Sant Bart comarca]] commissioner. The [[Archdiocese of Sant Bart]], the country's principal Catholic see, is also headquartered in the city.

== Transport ==

=== Metro ===

{{main|Metro de Sant Bart}}

[[File:Sant Bart Metro placeholder.jpg|thumb|280px|A Metro de Sant Bart train at a station in the city centre]]
